  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "---"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "# Design Plan: `capacity_refused` as an intelligible control signal"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "## 0. Key finding that drives the whole design (the load-bearing constraint)"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "`la_kind == \"capacity_refused\"` is **emitted from four distinct LA paths**, and the ratified mapping discipline says only **one** of them earns `new_authority_required`:"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "| Source | Location | ratified disposition |"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "|---|---|---|"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "| consume \u2192 `InsufficientCapacity` | `linear_accountant_client.py:816-829` | **`new_authority_required` / `current_grant`** \u2705 |"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "| request-time `Denied` | `linear_accountant_client.py:683-698` | `unknown` (must NOT be guessed) |"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "| unknown `CapacityDecision` variant | `linear_accountant_client.py:700-710` | `unknown` |"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "| unknown `ConsumptionDecision` variant | `linear_accountant_client.py:853-865` | `unknown` |"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "**Therefore the disposition cannot be derived downstream from `la_kind`** (all four look identical there). It must be assigned at the one structural branch where `InsufficientCapacity` is unambiguous \u2014 inside `consume()`. Der
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "A second consequence: the `no_session_grant` path in `lab_gate.py:162-167` sets `la_kind = self.grant_refusal`, which **can itself be `capacity_refused`** (a request-time `Denied` bubbling up). That path must default to `unknown` 
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "---"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "## 1. Where LA's decision becomes AG's worker-facing deny payload"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "Two hops:"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "1. **`linear_accountant_client.consume()`** (`linear_accountant_client.py:716-865`) maps the LA `ConsumptionDecision` \u2192 `RefusalResult(kind=\u2026)`."}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "2. **`lab_gate.decide_write_effect()`** (`lab_gate.py:148-202`) wraps that `RefusalResult` \u2192 `LabEffectDecision`."}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "3. **`SessionSupervisor._handle_tool_proposed()`** (`supervisor.py:617-638`) turns `LabEffectDecision` into (a) the `TOOL_CALL_DENIED` **bus event** payload and (b) the `ControlAction(kind=\"deny\", payload=\u2026)` that `adapter.
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "## 2. Are distinct LA refusal variants already preserved?"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "**Yes, for the non-`capacity_refused` variants** \u2014 `linear_accountant_client.py:836-851` already maps `Expired/Revoked/UnknownToken/ScopeMismatch` to their own closed kinds (`token_expired`, etc.) per the S4-lite ratification
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "**No, within the `capacity_refused` bucket** \u2014 the four sources above collapse to one `la_kind`. That collapse is exactly what blocks \"retry later vs. authority exhausted,\" and it is preserved only inside the branch structu
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "## 3. Minimum schema-bearing object"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "**Do not introduce a new wrapper dataclass.** Extend the two existing AG-side result types with three fields each, plus a closed enum defined alongside the existing `CLOSED_REFUSAL_KINDS`. This matches the repo's closed-vocab idio
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "New vocabulary (in `linear_accountant_client.py`, near line 124):"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "```python"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "RETRY_SAME_AUTHORITY     = \"retry_same_authority\""}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "RETRY_AFTER_DELAY        = \"retry_after_delay\""}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "NEW_AUTHORITY_REQUIRED   = \"new_authority_required\""}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "OPERATOR_ACTION_REQUIRED = \"operator_action_required\""}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "NEVER_RETRY              = \"never_retry\""}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "RETRY_UNKNOWN            = \"unknown\"          # default; NOT retry_after_delay"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "RETRY_DISPOSITIONS = frozenset({...all six...})"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "TERMINAL_SCOPE_CURRENT_GRANT = \"current_grant\""}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "CAPACITY_EXHAUSTED_MESSAGE = ("}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "    \"Write capacity for this grant is exhausted. \""}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "    \"Retrying under the same grant cannot succeed.\""}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": ")"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "```"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "Carriers (defaults make every existing call site valid unchanged):"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "- `RefusalResult` (`:257`): `+ retry_disposition: str = RETRY_UNKNOWN`, `+ terminal_scope: Optional[str] = None`, `+ message: Optional[str] = None`."}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "- `LabEffectDecision` (`lab_gate.py:68`): same three fields, same defaults."}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "**Agreement enforced by construction** (acceptance \u00a76) \u2014 extend `RefusalResult.__post_init__` (`:277-284`):"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "```python"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "if self.retry_disposition not in RETRY_DISPOSITIONS:"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "    raise ValueError(...)"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "if self.retry_disposition == NEW_AUTHORITY_REQUIRED:"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "    if not self.terminal_scope or not self.message:"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "        raise ValueError(\"new_authority_required requires terminal_scope and message\")"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "```"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "This makes \"machine fields and human text agree\" a cheap falsifiable invariant rather than a convention."}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "Reaches the worker via: `consume()` sets the fields \u2192 `decide_write_effect()` copies them \u2192 supervisor writes them into both the bus event payload and the `ControlAction.payload` delivered by `send_control`."}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "## 4. Backward-compatibility implications"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "- All three new fields have defaults \u2192 every existing positional/keyword construction of `RefusalResult` and `LabEffectDecision` stays valid."}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "- `la_kind`/`reason` are **untouched**: existing tests pinning `payload[\"la_kind\"] == \"capacity_refused\" | \"already_consumed\" | \"consumed\"` (`test_runtime_lab_gate.py:217,242,262`; `test_runtime_lab_gate_real_la.py:163-181
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "- The ratified schema's `reason` slot \u2261 AG's existing **`la_kind`** (the stable machine token); the ratified `message` is the **new** key. I deliberately do **not** rename `la_kind`\u2192`reason` or repurpose the existing pro
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "- Bus/ControlAction payloads are free-form dicts (`bus.emit(payload=\u2026)`), so added keys need no migration; consumers reading specific keys are unaffected."}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "- `__post_init__` is stricter, but only on the new field \u2014 defaults pass, so no existing construction newly raises."}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "## 5. Specific files + edits + tests"}
  [evt] agent_output :: {"text": "**Edit A \u2014 `src/governor/linear_accountant_client.py`**"}
